  "note": "Document-port bind and release (ticket 26/09/30/NON-DESTRUCTIVE-HISTORY-EDITING, live fault on build B1: attaching a fresh folder threw an unhandled `actor-document-control.receipt-count` out of the retirement of a binding that had failed to bind, the bind's own failure was lost, and every later bind of the program failed on that kept rejection). `answers` are what the program answers its control turns with, in order: `receipt` (the exact receipt, with a frame of the program's own riding beside it), `stale` (the refusal `plugin.document-backbone.stale-generation`: it holds no binding of that generation), `refused` (the refusal `plugin.document-backbone.binding-live`), `absent` (frames of its own, no receipt), `twice` (the receipt twice), `damaged` (a receipt with a byte after its end) and `transport` (the turn itself fails). `steps` are what the host does: `bind` (lets the predecessor go, then binds the next generation) and `retire` (retires the bound port). `outcomes` is how each step settles (`ok`, else the failure's message); `controls` are the control turns sent, as `<operation>:<generation>`; `told` are the retirement failures reported beside a failed bind.",
